@inherits RazorSlice

<section id="howto-content" class="content-card card border-0 shadow-sm">
    <div class="card-body p-4 p-xl-5">
        <div class="howto-step-header">
            <p class="card-kicker">Step 3</p>
            <h3 class="howto-step-title">Use a service as the feature composition root</h3>
        </div>

        <p class="section-summary howto-step-summary">The service should know how to build metadata, page definitions, and any additional feature-specific pieces. Endpoint modules stay thin when all feature composition happens there.</p>

        <ol class="howto-step-list">
            <li class="howto-step-item"><span class="howto-step-number">1</span><span class="howto-step-copy">Create `Features/{Feature}/Services/{Feature}ContentService.cs`.</span></li>
            <li class="howto-step-item"><span class="howto-step-number">2</span><span class="howto-step-copy">Add `CreateMetadata()` and `CreatePageDefinition()` methods.</span></li>
            <li class="howto-step-item"><span class="howto-step-number">3</span><span class="howto-step-copy">Keep nested feature decisions, default step selection, and helper methods in the service rather than inside endpoint classes.</span></li>
        </ol>

        <div class="howto-callout">
            <p class="card-kicker">Why this step exists</p>
            <p class="howto-callout-copy">This gives each feature one clear place where its page definition and internal behavior are assembled.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
